# Set X and Y Coordinates

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

When `x` coordinate values are omitted a cheater plot will be created. A carpet with only
`y:` has no `a`/`b` parameter values, so Plotly cannot lay out the grid: the chart below
intentionally shows **empty axes**. Add `a:` and `b:` arrays (see the "Add Parameter
Values" notebook) to draw it.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Carpet}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Carpet.new(
    y: [2, 3.5, 4, 3, 4.5, 5, 5.5, 6.5, 7.5, 8, 8.5, 10]
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Carpet Plot — Y Coordinates Only")
|> Plotly.show()
```
